    "id": "c7",
    "type": "comment",
    "name": "USEND / URCV with an S7 connection",
    "info": "The same S7 connection as for BSEND/BRCV (see the example 06): endpoint protocol 'S7 partner'.\n\ns7 urcv sends a message for each PLC USEND: msg.payload is a Buffer for one area (SD_1),\nan array of Buffers for two to four areas; msg.areas has the transport size of each area.\ns7 usend sends msg.payload to a PLC URCV with R_ID 4: one area or an array of up to four.\nAn S7-1500 URCV takes it only when each area has the exact length of its RD_i\n(here 8 bytes for an Array[0..7] of Byte). USEND has no acknowledgement.\nThe usend node writes to the PLC.",
